From: vegetableleaf <benzhu2029@u.northwestern.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] F1FIX-1: the Rune Giant's friend collector buffs its own
 troops: a filter name the tables do not hold reads as the Giant Buffer /
 Royal Chef row; hit_timer answered

The shipped giantbuffer_collect_friend_troops names TargetFilter friendly_troops_for_rune_giant, a row no table holds
(16.402.22 and 16.635.3). crforge read it as no filter, so its Rune Giant never found a friend, never fired
GiantBuffProjectile and never enchanted (no AddedDamage 86 every 3rd hit).
(c) for that reading: in 14 live matches (data 16.402 and 16.635) 136 of 136 enchant projectiles of the Rune Giant
went to an own troop, none to an enemy or a tower (SME-F1FIX rg_census.py / rg_filter.py; towers nearer than a
target were skipped 28 times). The name now reads as friendly_troops_for_chef_giant_buffer, the one filter of the
NO_GIANTBUFFER_CHEF_ENCHANTMENT tag ("units that can't be enchanted by GiantBuffer or Chef"); which exact filter the
game uses is (b).
Once friends are found, giantbuffer_no_move_on_buff asks hit_timer, which the battle refused. It now answers the
context's attack timer (0 while walking), untraced (b): 90 of 93 live launches made walking step on through the
600 ms; 2 pause about 600 ms, which no answer of 0 or more makes.
Test: aCollectorWithAMissingFilterBuffsAsTheGiantBufferRow replaces aCollectorWithAMissingFilterFindsNoFriend
(red on both data versions before; green after). Core: 16.635.3 2182/0 (6 skipped); 16.402.22 2182/0 (29 skipped).
